{"acceptanceTopology":{"candidatePath":"decisions/0006-phase-c-applicability-topology.json","implementationBoundary":"After the digest-specific decision-0006 receipt, one authority source commit may contain only the accepted authority, receipt, validator, and capture implementation. One evidence-only child commit must then append the zero-record twenty-successor authority-stage root before the authority PR can be ready or merge. No token materialization, Phase C capture, replacement PR, tracker decision-bearing mutation, or evidence acceptance occurs before the authority merge. After merge, issue #46 owns the implementation source commit followed by one evidence-only commit containing exactly six Phase C proof roots, their six Gate-owned successors from the authority-stage terminals, and the separate fourteen-successor non-proof maintenance root.","productScopePath":"strategy/product-scope.md","receiptPath":"decisions/0006-phase-c-applicability-topology-acceptance.json","requiredOwnerComment":"One authenticated ndrewtran comment on issue #39 must exactly match the validator-generated body and name and accept the exact Product Scope 4.0.1 and decision-0006 candidate paths, SHA-256 values, and byte lengths. Any byte change requires a new acceptance comment.","validator":"tooling/audits/repository-policy/src/phase-c-applicability-topology-correction-verify.mjs"},"affectedScopeIds":{"commitmentTransitions":"none; all 67 decision-0004/0005 affected Scope IDs remain committed and unchanged","count":67,"sha256":"sha256:c0c373a6efe0ca0355d7d6d6214dacc51a6f6a4c4c1c8a7fb61821663867eb65","sourceDecision":"core-ui:decision:0004"},"changeControlEffects":{"additions":"Two internal zero-record applicability roots: a pre-merge authority-stage root with exactly twenty successors required to keep the authority PR fail-closed, and a later non-proof maintenance root with exactly fourteen implementation-source successors. Neither is a product, package, public surface, evidence record, milestone root, Phase C root, advisory, exception, or release artifact.","authoring":"tests/ remains the sole owner of cross-package Phase C capture orchestration and emits the separate maintenance root from exact authority-owned target specifications. Package and tooling owners continue to author every product and applicability input.","migration":"No consumer or catalog migration changes. The proof-system transition is append-only in two explicit generations: preserve every existing byte; before authority merge append one successor to each of the twenty decision-0005 terminals; after the implementation source commit append one successor to each of those twenty authority-stage terminals, partitioned six plus fourteen.","packages":"No package, dependency, export, catalog, query, schema, command, token, renderer, or compatibility version changes.","platforms":"No platform behavior, support, accessibility, parity, availability, or renderer claim changes.","privacy":"The maintenance root contains only public-sanitized repository identities, hashes, assertion IDs, paths, timestamps, and the accepted decision reference. It contains no consumer, personal, device, prompt, screen, credential, or restricted evidence payload.","proof":"The pre-merge authority-stage root exists only to keep the accepted authority change applicable and has zero records. Later, the six Phase C roots remain the only replacement proof: their Gate root owns exactly six successors targeting the authority-stage continuations of the Phase-B indexes, while the separate maintenance root owns exactly fourteen source-drift successors and zero evidence records.","release":"No addition or removal from release scope and no package publication or release claim.","rollback":"Before capture, rollback is omission of the uncommitted evidence-only output. After append-only capture, no certificate or root is deleted or rewritten; a later accepted authority/source drift may append at most one new digest-linked successor per terminal chain.","security":"Decision and receipt identities, exact predecessor hashes, source commit/tree, historical indexes, assertion arrays, path manifests, and terminal uniqueness fail closed. No bypass, waiver, network fallback, or mutable latest-state lookup is admitted."},"decisionId":"core-ui:decision:0006","deferredCurrentStateProjection":{"disposition":"deferred","effect":"none on Phase C","reason":"A deterministic current-state projection may later reduce navigation noise but is not required to preserve or verify the append-only evidence chains and is not admitted by this correction."},"fieldOwnership":{"authored":["acceptanceTopology","affectedScopeIds","changeControlEffects","deferredCurrentStateProjection","nonGoals","observedProblem","proofTopology","roadmapImpact","supersession","trackerMigration","validation","versions"],"derived":["future implementation source commit/tree","future current applicability-manifest hashes","certificate and index content hashes","evidence-only commit/tree"],"proofRequired":["exact twenty-successor authority-stage generation before authority merge","exact six-plus-fourteen terminal partition after the implementation source commit","each generation uses one common exact source commit/tree and the decision-0006 receipt","six and only six Phase C evidence roots","zero evidence records in both applicability-only roots","historical byte preservation","capture/check byte identity for both capture scripts","stale-terminal rejection after each generation"],"referenced":["architecture EvidenceApplicabilitySupersession contract","decision 0005 and acceptance receipt","the twenty terminal authority-39-default-theme-identity certificates","the six accepted Phase-B index digests","the six decision-0005 Phase C root paths"]},"humanDecisionOwner":"ndrewtran","nonGoals":["adding a seventh Phase C evidence root or changing any Phase C assertion","using the maintenance root as evidence, acceptance, support, promotion, release, or milestone proof","continuing the six Phase-B chains in the maintenance root","continuing the fourteen non-Phase-B chains in the Phase C Gate root","targeting the authority-39-default-theme-identity container index instead of its exact terminal certificates","weakening stale-current-manifest rejection or adding a pending-status bypass","rewriting or deleting any historical evidence or authority byte","changing tokens, packages, schemas, queries, renderers, compatibility, or release identities","implementing a deterministic current-state projection","claiming Phase C, G1.0, G1.1, Gate 1, package, or release acceptance"],"observedProblem":{"currentTerminalCount":20,"gateAuthorizedPhaseBSuccessorCount":6,"reason":"Decision 0005 correctly created twenty terminal authority-expiry certificates. The accepted Phase C Gate topology authorizes successors for only the six Phase-B chains. The implementation source changes every terminal current applicability manifest because their path sets include changed source and repository-policy paths. Without an accepted owner for the remaining fourteen successors, deterministic verification must reject those stale terminal manifests. The decision-0006 authority change itself also changes governed Product Scope and repository-policy paths, so it requires a first accepted successor generation before that authority PR can merge; the later implementation then requires a second generation.","uncoveredTerminalCount":14},"parentDecision":{"acceptancePath":"decisions/0005-default-theme-token-source-identity-acceptance.json","acceptanceSha256":"sha256:48ac9f5af1990743224ab8fbdf093d08c092268842714a7d238a7d21b03c5c57","decisionId":"core-ui:decision:0005","decisionPath":"decisions/0005-default-theme-token-source-identity.json","decisionSha256":"sha256:747eb372d7cb53351d1cc30f4092cd703feb7986d3ea12814da6974616b85262"},"proofTopology":{"authorityStage":{"captureScript":"tests/evidence/capture-authority-39-phase-c-applicability-topology-supersessions